From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 09:33:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/m720q_m920q: The VR power delivery design of the
 OEM firmware

FSP-S takes the current limits and load lines of the processor's
voltage regulators from a table of Intel's board designs when
VrPowerDeliveryDesign names one, and keeps generic values with 0, the
default coreboot passed. The Lenovo firmware of these boards (M1UKT,
for the M720q, M920q and M920x) sets 11, CFL_S_35_WATT_8_2: all three
copies of its Setup variable in the flash of an M920x have it, the last
one saved with a 65 W i3-8100 (PL2 81.25 W), so it follows the board
and not the processor. Set the same.

TEST=On the M920x with the i3-8100 (ci-166 against ci-169): the same
within the noise, idle 0.81 and 0.79 W, under a load on all four cores
for 60 s 44.61 and 44.64 W at 1.1205 and 1.1213 V, 3599 MHz, stable.
The table matters at the current limits of the processors with more
cores, which these boards also take; the gain for those is the OEM's
validated values, not a measurement here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb
index 9b19d1e419..4a83c3401f 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb
@@ -18,6 +18,12 @@ chip soc/intel/cannonlake
 	# SATA Power Optimizer, off by default in FSP-S
 	register "satapwroptimize" = "true"
 
+	# The voltage regulator design of these boards, as the OEM firmware
+	# sets it whatever the processor (its saved setup: 11, also with a
+	# 65 W one): CFL_S_35_WATT_8_2, Intel's VR current and load line
+	# values for it. 0, the default, keeps the generic values of FSP-S
+	register "VrPowerDeliveryDesign" = "11"
+
 	# Wake on LAN from S4 and S5, as the OEM firmware (the "wake_on_lan" option)
 	register "WolEnableOverride" = "true"
 
-- 
